                <pb facs="0348" n="220" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg220"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Article</hi> 8 <hi rendition="#italic">of law</hi> 53
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of</hi> 1884, <hi rendition="#italic">to which the
                        preceding decree, No</hi>. 636, <hi rendition="#italic">refers</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 8. The Executive is hereby authorized to
                    establish custom houses in Panama, Colon, Aranca, and Oracué. The personal of
                    the service thereof shall not exceed the salaries paid at the custom-house at
                    Santa Martha.</p>
                <pb facs="0349" n="221" xml:id="pg221"/>
                <p>The duties collected at the new ports named shall he those provided for in the
                    existing tariff laws, less 40 per cent.</p>
                <p>The executive decree organizing the customs service at said new ports shall he
                    submitted to the next succeeding session of Congress.</p>
            </div>
